### (1) ###
class Test
{
  static int i;
  int j;
};

int Test::i;

----> static data members do not contribute in size of an object. So 'i' is not considered in size of Test. 
      Also, all functions (static and non-static both) do not contribute in size.

### (2) ###
class Base1 {  Base1() }
class Base2 {  Base2() }

class Derived: public Base1, public Base{ }

----> Base1's constructor called ---> Base2's constructor called ---> Derived's constructor called .  In case of Multiple Inheritance, 
      constructors of base classes are always called in derivation order from -> left to right  
      Destructors are called in reverse order. 
